WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.610
- I know that I've talked to
you about your album a lot.

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:03.443
I know.

00:00:03.443 --> 00:00:04.276
- You can keep going.

00:00:04.276 --> 00:00:06.656
I actually enjoy it.
- You probably think

00:00:06.656 --> 00:00:07.489
I'm psychotic at this point

00:00:07.489 --> 00:00:08.322
(laughing)

00:00:08.322 --> 00:00:09.290
Literally every time I see him at the show

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:10.550
I'm like, "Dude."

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:11.383
I was like, "I can't."

00:00:11.383 --> 00:00:13.357
And this is a testimony, I told you this.

00:00:13.357 --> 00:00:14.240
- [John] Do you have a favorite song?

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.850
- Oh my gosh, I mean,
I love "Wild" actually,

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.011
which you're gonna be performing today.

00:00:19.011 --> 00:00:19.844
- Yes.

00:00:19.844 --> 00:00:21.970
- But "Favorite Place",
I'm really into "Ooh Laa"

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:23.427
I really love, I love the whole album,

00:00:23.427 --> 00:00:24.260
"Conversations in the Dark"

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.430
I love the whole thing, it's so, so great.

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:27.980
- Those songs are kind of sexy songs.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:28.842
- Dude, I know, that's what I'm saying.

00:00:28.842 --> 00:00:29.675
(laughing)

00:00:29.675 --> 00:00:30.680
This is a testament of
how good this album is.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.760
I started the show with saying
like, "Hey, my personal life

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:33.593
is kind of like, ha ha."

00:00:33.593 --> 00:00:34.426
(loud huff)

00:00:34.426 --> 00:00:35.600
And so, I'm just saying,

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.920
if this album can be so
great for someone like me,

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.560
that's really wanting some Joni Mitchell,

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:41.393
Alanis Morrisette at this point.

00:00:41.393 --> 00:00:42.226
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:42.226 --> 00:00:43.390
- Like it's a great album.

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:44.223
- Well, thank you.

00:00:44.223 --> 00:00:48.170
I truly, you know, we
all work in this business

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:51.030
and so, we can be a
little jaded and cynical.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:52.520
- I know I'm never like this with albums.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.590
- And for another artist to
actually care about your music

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:57.980
and listen to it and love
it and really pay attention,

00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:58.950
it really does mean a lot.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:01.480
So I am truly grateful
for your compliments

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:03.070
and they're not getting old to me.

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:03.958
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:01:03.958 --> 00:01:04.897
(laughing)

00:01:04.897 --> 00:01:06.323
you're probably like, "Calm down."

00:01:06.323 --> 00:01:09.060
It just makes me happy, I love it.

